# =============================================================================
# selective_import — selective value imports (EBNF rows [067] importa_sugar /
# [071] selective_import / [072] import_value_binding).
# =============================================================================
#
# What this teaches:
#   • Value bindings — `importa ex "norma:console" fixum write_partial ut output,
#     write_bytes ut output_bytes` imports one exported value member per `fixum`
#     local; the pre-`ut` identifier names an exported value in the imported
#     file, the post-`ut` identifier is the caller-owned local binding
#   • Values and types — functions and constants bind as values; a type
#     export binds the type itself, usable in type positions exactly like
#     its qualified `module.Type` path (it is not a value, and `est` against
#     it is rejected until cross-file type tests are designed)
#   • Ordinary locals — the bindings obey ordinary local-binding rules
#     (duplicates, shadowing, lints), are locale-resolved through the
#     imported module, and are never re-exports
#   • No wildcard mixing — wildcard members cannot mix into the selective
#     list; `publica` before `fixum` re-exports each binding
#   • Trailing comma — the current parser tolerates one trailing comma after
#     the final member; the canonical spine keeps every comma required
#   • Callable values — an imported function binds as an ordinary callable
#     local, so it can be passed or called like any other function value
#
# Common mistakes:
#   • expecting a type binding to be a value — `nota Type` or `x est Type`
#     on an imported type is an error
#   • expecting the bindings to re-export — only `publica` bindings do
#
# See also: importa, ex
# =============================================================================

importa ex "norma:console" fixum write_partial ut output, write_bytes ut output_bytes

functio scribe((textus) → vacuum sink, textus nomen) → vacuum {
    sink(nomen)
}

incipit {
    sit textus nomen ← "salve"
    nota nomen
}
